{"body":"## Problem\n\nThe active governance rule set is inconsistent across the public/bootstrap sources.\n\nFrom the site/repo review:\n\n- `bootstrap.json` appears to list active rules only through `gov-09-agent-continuity-bootstrap`.\n- `agent.txt` also refers to GOV-01 through GOV-09 as the active set.\n- The published governance documentation/sidebar includes GOV-01 through GOV-13.\n- Release history indicates GOV-10 through GOV-13 exist as harness-engineering governance rules.\n\nThis creates ambiguity for agents and users: should GOV-10 to GOV-13 be installed, ignored, treated as preview, or treated as optional extensions?\n\nBecause VibeGov is itself a governance source of truth, this mismatch undermines trust in the bootstrap contract.\n\n## Affected areas\n\nLikely affected files/outputs:\n\n- `static/bootstrap.json`\n- `static/agent.txt`\n- `docs/bootstrap` / bootstrap contract docs\n- published governance docs/sidebar\n- any bootstrap validation assumptions\n- release notes or rule index pages if they describe the active set\n\n## Recommended fix\n\nDecide one clear rule-set status:\n\n### Preferred option\n\nMake GOV-01 through GOV-13 the active published rule set everywhere.\n\nUpdate active rule references to include:\n\n- `gov-10-agent-state-closure-git-hygiene`\n- `gov-11-agent-legibility-in-repo-truth`\n- `gov-12-drift-control-garbage-collection`\n- `gov-13-review-loops-completion-discipline`\n\n### Alternative option\n\nIf GOV-10 to GOV-13 are not intended to be core yet, clearly label them as one of:\n\n- extended rules\n- preview rules\n- optional harness rules\n- experimental rules\n\nThen make the docs/sidebar reflect that status.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `bootstrap.json` and `agent.txt` agree on the active rule set.\n- [ ] Bootstrap docs use the same rule range/status as the machine-readable sources.\n- [ ] Published docs/sidebar clearly distinguish active vs optional/preview rules if applicable.\n- [ ] A new user or agent can determine exactly which rules should be installed during bootstrap.\n- [ ] No public page implies GOV-10 to GOV-13 are active while machine-readable sources omit them, or vice versa.\n\n## Priority\n\nP0 — source-of-truth consistency.","id":"PVTI_lADOA_2mn84Bc1k8zgyJwBA","title":"Align active governance rule set across bootstrap sources","type":"Issue","url":"https://github.com/governance-foundation/vibegov.io/issues/154"}